     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I don&#39;t know how plot.image() works internally, but if it instructs the graphics driver to paint thousands of filled squares, this is what the graphics driver does -- and in the case of tikzDevice this results in a huge file.<div><br></div><div>I don&#39;t remember such issues with ggplot2/grid graphics, so you may want to try an alternative method of producing the plots.<div><br></div><div><br></div><div>-Kirill</div></div></div>"
